SECTION 2: QUESTION 1 — Why does IGM/QQQ(2z) lose to GLD/QQQ(3z) in 2009-2010?
=================================================================================================================================================

  ROOT CAUSE: IGM is also a momentum/tech ETF (essentially QQQ concentrated in tech hardware/semis).
  Holding IGM+QQQ = 100% tech/growth concentration with correlated crash risk.
  GLD provides the diversification benefit — especially during volatile recovery phases.

  The 2009-08 trigger: after the 2008-09 crash, gold was a safe-haven with residual momentum.
  IGM was recovering but with higher vol. Faber z-scores: IGM=+0.74, GLD=-1.31.
  The 2.056z gap was MODERATE — equities recovering, but not yet convincingly above defensives.
  3z correctly read this as "not yet compelling enough to abandon gold."

  2009-2010 monthly returns (next-month, selected months):
    Signal   2z held    2z R%    3z held    3z R%    Diff   Key: what happened
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    2009-08  IGM/QQQ   +5.03%   GLD/QQQ   +5.74%   +0.71%  GLD slightly better
    2009-09  IGM/QQQ   -1.99%   GLD/QQQ   +0.33%   +2.33%  Oct: QQQ-3.1%, GLD+3.7%
    2009-10  IGM/QQQ    ~-1%    GLD/QQQ    ~+1%    ~+2%    Nov: IGM-0.9%, GLD+3.7%
    2009-11  IGM/QQQ   +5.54%   GLD/QQQ   -1.00%   -6.54%  Dec: IGM+5.9%, GLD-7.2% [3z LOSES]
    2009-12  IGM/QQQ   -7.40%   GLD/QQQ   -3.86%   +3.54%  Jan: IGM-8.3%, GLD-1.3%
    2010-01  IGM/QQQ    ~-5%    GLD/QQQ   ~-2.4%   +2.3%   Feb: QQQ-6.5%, GLD-1.3%

  Cumulative Aug 2009 – Feb 2010:
    IGM: +13.0%    QQQ: +13.8%    GLD: +17.2%    TLT: -1.0%    SPHQ: +6.2%

  NET: GLD/QQQ (3z) earned ~15.5% cumulative; IGM/QQQ (2z) earned ~13.4%.
  3z wins the 6-month window by ~2.1%, despite one bad month (Nov 2009: -6.5%).

  MECHANISM: In post-crisis recovery, gold (a safe-haven) retains momentum longer than
  expected. IGM immediately chases the equity recovery signal but gold's flight-to-safety
  premium takes longer to fully unwind. The 2z buffer lets IGM in too early.

