SECTION 4: QUESTION 3 — Why does 2z=3z post-2015?
=================================================================================================================================================

  Z-SCORE DISTRIBUTION BY SUBWINDOW:
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Period       z_range   gap_top1v2   gap_top2v3   n_pos_candidates
    2008-2014     3.772       0.665        0.428          10.4
    2015-2019     3.593       0.395        0.302          10.6   ← COMPRESSED
    2020-2026     3.677       0.717        0.362          10.9
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  CANDIDATE SET STABILITY (Jaccard month-over-month):
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Period       avg_jaccard   avg_new_entrants/mo
    2008-2014      0.680             1.27
    2015-2019      0.641             1.32
    2020-2026      0.686             1.25
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  → Candidate stability is UNCHANGED across periods. Pool churn is similar.
    The post-2015 identity is NOT explained by pool stabilization.

  THE REAL ANSWER: Gap distribution between candidate #1 and #2 compressed in 2015-2019.

  MECHANISM: The [2z,3z) TRIGGER BAND requires a specific market configuration:
    1. Current holding: defensive (TLT/GLD) with MODERATE z-score (not strongly positive)
    2. Challenger: risk-on asset with MODERATELY higher z-score
    3. The gap between them falls in [2,3z) — real signal but not overwhelming

  This configuration occurs during REGIME TRANSITIONS (crash → recovery, growth → risk-off)
  where momentum signals are genuinely ambiguous. Post-2015 bull market (2015-2019) had
  a specific characteristic: assets cluster at similar momentum levels (gap_top1v2=0.395).

  When top assets cluster (small inter-asset z-gaps):
    → z_swap - z_prior is more likely to be SMALL (<2z) → both buffers keep → identical
    → OR very large (>3z) when a NEW asset clearly dominates → both buffers swap → identical
    → The [2z,3z) middle zone is rarely hit because the market rarely produces
      "moderately convincing but not overwhelmingly convincing" momentum differences
      in a steady bull market environment

  Year 2017 gap_top1v2=0.178 — extreme compression. Top 2 assets nearly tied in Faber z.
  In this environment, z_swap - z_prior almost never reaches 2z, let alone 3z.

  POST-2019: 2019-12 DID trigger (gap=2.411). This was the COVID pre-shock environment
  where TLT had z=-2.11 (very depressed) and VEA z=+0.30. Classic regime transition.
  The 2020-2026 gap_top1v2=0.717 is wide (mostly driven by 2022: gap1v2=1.907 in the
  bond-crash year), consistent with higher trigger probability — but states reconverged
  by March 2020, and no new triggers occurred from 2020-2026 in the study.

