SECTION 6: QUESTION 5-6 — Z-score range vs candidate set stability
=================================================================================================================================================

  Q5: Does z-score RANGE shrink post-2015?
  ANSWER: NO. z_range stays 3.5-4.2 consistently. The OVERALL spread doesn't compress.

  What DOES compress: gap_top1v2 (separation between RANK #1 and RANK #2 candidates).
    2008-2014: 0.665z   →   2015-2019: 0.395z   →   2020-2026: 0.717z

  This means in 2015-2019, the top-2 candidates are nearly tied in relative momentum.
  But the bottom of the universe still spreads far below. So z_range = similar.

  Q6: Does candidate POOL stabilize post-2015?
  ANSWER: NO. Jaccard and new entrant counts are essentially UNCHANGED (0.64-0.69, 1.25-1.32/mo).
  Pool churn is constant. The convergence is NOT because "the same assets always win."

  CONCLUSION: Post-2015 2z=3z identity is caused by z-score CLUSTERING among top
  candidates (gap1v2 compressed), not by pool stabilization or range compression.

