SECTION 8: ACTIONABLE CONCLUSIONS
=================================================================================================================================================

  1. USE 3z IN PRODUCTION — justified but with realistic expectations
     - Mechanism is economically coherent (don't swap defensives on moderate signal)
     - Lower transaction costs independently support higher buffer
     - Forward Sharpe advantage estimate: +0.05 to +0.10 (not +0.20)
     - Trust the mechanism, not the specific numerical advantage

  2. THE 2z vs 3z DEBATE IS MOSTLY ABOUT ONE EVENT
     - 2012-05 (+7.7%) from the 2012-03 trigger (gap=2.938z) = ~40% of the 18y advantage
     - If you anchored to 2z, you'd avoid this overfit risk but lose the mechanism benefit
     - Both are defensible. 3z is slightly better in expectation but not by the full 0.20

  3. WHY 2z=3z POST-2015 (the simple answer)
     - 2015-2019 US bull market: equity factors had high stable z-scores
     - When equities dominated, they did so OVERWHELMINGLY (>3z gap) or not at all
     - The "moderate signal" regime that produces [2z,3z) gaps is a CRISIS TRANSITION pattern
     - Post-2020 reconverged by March 2020; no further triggers through 2026-05

  4. FORWARD WATCH SIGNAL
     - If FCP again holds TLT or GLD, and equity factor builds moderate (not overwhelming)
       Faber momentum → the [2z,3z) zone will be tested again
     - This tends to happen in early recovery from shocks or late-cycle tension
     - When it fires, 3z will block the rotation. The next year's performance will reveal
       whether it was another correct call or the first 3z miss

  5. ROBUSTNESS HEDGE: if you want to reduce overfit exposure while keeping mechanism:
     - Use HOLD_BUFFER=2.5z (Sh=1.095 live, lower sensitivity to the 2.938 event)
     - Accept -0.10 Sharpe versus 3z, in exchange for threshold not coincidentally
       matching a single historical event so tightly
     - The 2.5z result (1.095) still beats 2z (0.968) by 0.127 Sharpe on genuine mechanism

